{
  "status": "success",
  "app_url": "http://localhost:3000",
  "start_command": "npm run dev",
  "summary": "A single-user book tracker for a home library: add books with title, author, and kind; lend them out to a named person; mark them returned; edit or delete entries; filter to see only books currently out; and see how many are lent out right now. Data persists in the browser.",
  "implemented_features": [
    "Add a book with title, author, and category (Novel, Cookbook, Reference, etc.)",
    "See all books in one list, sorted by title",
    "Lend a book out by recording the borrower's name",
    "Mark a borrowed book as returned",
    "Edit an existing book's title, author, or category",
    "Delete a mistakenly added book (with confirmation)",
    "Filter the list to only books currently out with someone",
    "Derived count: how many of the total books are lent out right now",
    "Persistence across refresh via browser localStorage",
    "Recovery from malformed persisted data",
    "Input validation and trimming for empty/whitespace input"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The idea lists example categories (novel, cookbook, reference) but is open-ended; I provide a fixed, inclusive category list ending in 'Other' rather than free-text categories, to keep the kind-of-book field consistent and selectable. 'Other' covers anything not enumerated.",
    "A book is considered 'currently out' when it has a non-empty borrower; there is no separate borrow-date concept because the idea asks only to note who has what and clear it on return.",
    "Returning a book clears the borrower but keeps the book on the shelf; the idea treats lending as a state of the book, not a separate loan record.",
    "Single user, single device, no login or shared access is implied; data lives only in this browser's localStorage.",
    "Deletion is permanent and confirmed via a native confirm dialog; no undo is required by the idea."
  ],
